  <LocalizationPair Name="%AcademyRoleLibrarianDescription">With access to both ancient and recent studies and data, the Librarian can find answers to difficult questions, discover advanced technologies, and highly effectively infiltrate networks.</LocalizationPair>
  <LocalizationPair Name="%AcademyRoleLibrarianEffectOverride">The Librarian can access hidden information only available to the Academy, such as data on the state of heroes and other empires, critical hacking vulnerabilities in network protocols, and a cache of scientific information enabling the research of technologies one stage higher than normal.</LocalizationPair>
  <LocalizationPair Name="%AcademyRoleGrandAdmiralDescription">The Spear of Isyander is the leader of the Academy fleets and personally directs one of the largest, as well as gaining access to Academy gunners and squadron pilots.</LocalizationPair>
  <LocalizationPair Name="%AcademyRoleGrandAdmiralEffectOverride">The Spear of Isyander may command the Academy attack Master Fleet directly, and gains +5% module damage per unlocked military era.</LocalizationPair>
  <LocalizationPair Name="%AcademyRoleVaultKeeperDescription">The Vault Keeper does not guard Academy treasures, but manages a vast, secure infrastructure that tracks the rules and regulations of the galaxy. This position confers increased political prominence.</LocalizationPair>
  <LocalizationPair Name="%AcademyRoleVaultKeeperEffectOverride">The Vault Keeper has access to all the laws of an additional party of his choice (with the exception of the super-law), and influence radius gains are increased by 10% empire-wide.</LocalizationPair>
  <LocalizationPair Name="%DiplomaticInteractionAppeasementForcedPeaceFromColdWarAfraidVaulters">I expected fleets of ships, not an offer of peace. I will not hide the Aurigans' feeling of relief.</LocalizationPair>
  <LocalizationPair Name="%TechnologyDefinitionEmpireDevelopment13Description">The construction of nano-machines--or nanites--capable of operating in liquid environments with various conditions of salinity, temperature, pressure, and microbial life has a range of potential applications. Research into energy sources, locomotion, and self-repair enables a whole ecology of these liquid nanites to be developed.</LocalizationPair>
